# NOTE (2026-08-02): This workspace is synced by Google Drive (Mirror mode), NOT git — so this
# .gitignore governs NOTHING at runtime. It is retained only as a human-readable record of which
# paths are meant to stay off the cloud. The actual enforcement is NOT this file and is NOT an
# in-folder exclusion: Google Drive for Desktop mirrors a folder whole and cannot skip a subfolder
# inside it. Instead, the research agent keeps raw/large/restricted data in a LOCAL-ONLY folder
# OUTSIDE the mirrored workspace (e.g. ~/research-data-local/<workspace>/), so it never syncs at all.
# See data/README.md → "What's synced vs. local — and how the split works."
#
# articles/ (copyrighted reference PDFs) now SYNC with the workspace — under the student-owned-Drive
# model they are personal-use copies in the student's own Drive, and syncing lets them follow the
# student across machines. (Earlier git-based setups excluded them to avoid redistribution in a
# shared repo; that concern is gone under per-student Drive.)
articles/*
!articles/README.md

# Raw research data does NOT live here — it is staged in a local-only folder outside the mirrored
# workspace (see data/README.md). These patterns record the intent only; they enforce nothing.
data/raw/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep
data/*.csv
data/*.dta
data/*.sav
data/*.parquet

# macOS / editor noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
